{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 6, :comments ["<b>And I will make it a waste.</b> Like שממה, and like it in 'streams of the wastes' (Isaiah 7:19)." "<b>It shall not be pruned.</b> From the root of זמורה, its proper sense being to cut the branch from it." "<b>It shall be hoed.</b> Proper usage, like חפירה, and like it in 'which with a hoe they shall hoe' (Isaiah 7:25)." "<b>Briers and thorns.</b> Kinds of thorns, and the meaning is that the wicked shall prevail." "And the meaning of <b>upon the clouds</b> is upon the prophets, and so it is written: 'Her prophets also find no vision' (Lamentations 2:9)."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 5, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:52:17.303606406Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}